&lt;p&gt;Hi, we&#39;re Oscar. We&#39;re hiring a Technical Program Manager, Data to join our Technical PMO team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is the first health insurance company built around a full stack technology platform and a relentless focus on serving our members. We started Oscar in 2012 to create the kind of health insurance company we would want for ourselves—one that behaves like a doctor in the family.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead the data transformation at the core of realizing better healthcare for millions of people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is hiring a Technical Program Manager to join our Tech PMO, dedicated to a major enterprise data transformation. You’ll partner closely with Data leadership to lead migration from planning through delivery, protecting the quality and integrity of the data our teams rely on every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who has experience partnering with Data teams and leading a major enterprise data migration and who brings curiosity, initiative, and sound judgment. You can engage deeply with business partners, data scientists, data engineers, make complex dependencies and tradeoffs clear, and help leaders make timely decisions. You take ownership of execution while building trust with the people who produce and use the data.&lt;br&gt;Your program will include revamping our data transformation and semantic layers, as well as evolving our data governance and data quality capabilities across the entire business. You’ll coordinate Analytics Engineering, Data Engineering, Data Scientists, Analysts, and business owners through migration, validation, adoption, and operational handoff.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll have the opportunity to shape how Oscar delivers enterprise data programs and help build a strong TPM team. This is an individual contributor role reporting to the Director of the Tech PMO, partnering closely with Data leadership. You’ll lead technical program execution, with Data Engineering accountable for architecture and implementation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report into the Director, Technical Program Management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location: &lt;/strong&gt;This position is based in our New York City office, requiring a hybrid work schedule with 3 days of in-office work per week. Thursdays are a required in-office day for team meetings and events, while your other two office days are flexible to suit your schedule. #LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency: &lt;/strong&gt;The base pay for this role is: $&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;117,576 -&lt;/span&gt; $&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;154,319 &lt;/span&gt;per year. You are also eligible for employee benefits, participation in Oscar&#39;s unlimited vacation program, and annual performance bonuses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the integrated enterprise data migration plan from scoping through delivery and operational handoff, with clear owners, migration waves, milestones, dependencies, and acceptance criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn ambiguity into action across dbt migration, Cube implementation, data governance, and data quality workstreams. Bring the right owners together and resolve gaps in scope, sequencing, and readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Analytics Engineering, Data Engineering, Data Scientists, Analysts, and business owners to map upstream and downstream dependencies, coordinate commitments, and make scope, sequencing, and capacity tradeoffs explicit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate migration risks and drive timely decisions. Escalate with clear options, recommendations, and impact on data quality, integrity, reporting, and business continuity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate data reconciliation, testing, cutover and rollback plans, adoption, and operational readiness. Ensure technical and business owners agree on validation evidence, go/no-go criteria, and required security, privacy, and compliance reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support program planning and give Data and executive leaders a clear view of migration progress, readiness, unresolved decisions, and outcomes. Drive business acceptance and clear operational ownership for migrated domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build a strong TPM team: share useful practices, challenge unnecessary processes, support colleagues, and turn lessons from delivery into improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance with all applicable laws and regulations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of technical program or project management/process-oriented operations work experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience using coding languages such as SQL to analyze project performance and risks and develop erports for management and business owners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience independently leading complex software development programs across multiple teams, from planning through launch and operational handoff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency in data pipelines, transformation layers, data models, semantic layers, lineage, and integrations, with the judgment to challenge migration plans, validation approaches, and implementation tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to structure ambiguous enterprise programs, manage cross-domain dependencies and competing priorities, and coordinate data validation, cutover readiness, and business continuity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A record of building trust and influencing decisions across Analytics Engineering, Data Engineering, Data Scientists, Analysts, and business owners, and executive stakeholders without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication, including the ability to translate technical migration risks into business impact and recommend a course of action to senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership and follow-through, with examples of moving work forward when plans change or obstacles arise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in healthcare, health insurance, or another regulated industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with dbt and Cube, or comparable transformation and semantic-layer technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing data governance, data quality controls, lineage, or consistent business metric definitions across domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating external vendors and helping business and analytics teams adopt new data platforms and ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience migrating business-critical analytics or reporting with staged validation, reconciliation, cutover, and rollback practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This is an authentic Oscar Health job opportunity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Oscar, being an Equal Opportunity Employer means more than upholding discrimination-free hiring practices. It means that we cultivate an environment where people can be their most authentic selves and find both belonging and support. We&#39;re on a mission to change health care -- an experience made whole by our unique backgrounds and perspectives.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency:&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Final offer amounts, within the base pay set forth above, are determined by factors including your relevant skills, education, and experience. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Full-time employees are eligible for benefits including: medical, dental, and vision benefits, 11 paid holidays, paid sick time, paid parental leave, 401(k) plan participation, life and disability insurance, and paid wellness time and reimbursements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Artificial Intelligence (AI): &lt;/strong&gt;Our &lt;a href=&quot;https://oscarhealth.com/careers/ai-guidelines&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AI Guidelines&lt;/a&gt; outline the acceptable use of artificial intelligence for candidates and detail how we use AI to support our recruiting efforts.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasonable Accommodation: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Oscar applicants are considered solely based on their qualifications, without regard to applicant’s disability or need for accommodation. Any Oscar applicant who requires reasonable accommodations during the application process should contact the Oscar Benefits Team (accommodations@hioscar.com) to make the need for an accommodation known.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;California Residents:&lt;/strong&gt; For information about our collection, use, and disclosure of applicants’ personal information as well as applicants’ rights over their personal information, please see our &lt;a href=&quot;https://oscarhealth.com/privacy-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Hi, we&#39;re Oscar. We&#39;re hiring Technical Program Managers to join our Technical Program Management team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is the first health insurance company built around a full stack technology platform and a relentless focus on serving our members. We started Oscar in 2012 to create the kind of health insurance company we would want for ourselves—one that behaves like a doctor in the family.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help turn ambitious plans into better healthcare experiences through technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is hiring three Technical Program Managers to join our growing Technology Program Management Office (Tech PMO). By applying to this job post, you will be considered for all Technical Program Manager openings. Specific role placement will be determined following the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Technical Program Manager, you will lead work that helps members navigate their coverage, providers work more easily with Oscar, clinical teams deliver better care, and grow our business.&amp;nbsp;We’re looking for someone who brings curiosity, initiative, and sound judgment. You enjoy understanding how systems work, asking thoughtful questions, and finding a path forward when the answer isn’t obvious. You build trust across teams, make difficult tradeoffs clear, and follow through on the details that turn a good plan into a successful launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll partner with Product, Engineering, and business leaders across our Network, Growth, Member, and Clinical pillars. Each hire will support a defined set of teams, combining visibility across their roadmaps with direct leadership of selected complex programs. Your work could span provider data platforms, clinical integrations, member digital experiences, enrollment, broker tools, or marketing technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an early member of a growing Tech PMO, you’ll also help shape how we plan, solve problems, and deliver together. This is an individual contributor role reporting to the Director of the Tech PMO.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report into the Director, Technical Program Management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is based in our New York City office, requiring a hybrid work schedule with 3 days of in-office work per week. Thursdays are a required in-office day for team meetings and events, while your other two office days are flexible to suit your schedule. #LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base pay for this role is: $117,576.00 - $154,318.50 per year. You are also eligible for employee benefits, participation in Oscar&#39;s unlimited vacation program, and annual performance bonuses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex technical programs from scoping through launch and operational handoff. Build integrated plans with clear owners, milestones, dependencies, and measures of success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn ambiguity into action. Bring the right people together, clarify the problem, and establish practical next steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Engineering, and business leaders to connect roadmaps, coordinate commitments, and make scope, sequencing, and capacity tradeoffs explicit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate delivery risks and resolve dependency gaps. Drive timely decisions and escalate with clear options, recommendations, and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate teams and vendors through integrations, testing, adoption, and launch readiness, including required security, privacy, and compliance reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support quarterly and annual planning. Give leaders a clear view of progress, what needs attention, and whether delivered work is producing the intended results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build a strong TPM team: share useful practices, challenge unnecessary process, support colleagues, and turn lessons from delivery into improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance with all applicable laws and regulations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of technical program or project management/process-oriented operations work experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience using coding languages such as SQL to analyze project performance and risks and develop erports for management and business owners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience independently leading complex software development programs across multiple teams, from planning through launch and operational handoff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency to engage engineers on software systems, APIs, data flows, integrations, and implementation tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to bring structure to ambiguous problems and manage dependencies, risks, and competing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A record of building trust and influencing decisions across technical and business teams without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication, including the ability to explain complex issues and recommend a course of action to senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership and follow-through, with examples of moving work forward when plans change or obstacles arise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree 4 years commensurate experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in healthcare, health insurance, or another regulated industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in one or more relevant areas: provider platforms, clinical systems, consumer digital products, enrollment, broker or distribution platforms, or marketing technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with external vendors, platform migrations, or complex system integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience improving planning and delivery practices or helping teams adopt new tools and ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering AI-enabled products or workflow automation, including evaluation and operational readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This is an authentic Oscar Health job opportunity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Oscar, being an Equal Opportunity Employer means more than upholding discrimination-free hiring practices. It means that we cultivate an environment where people can be their most authentic selves and find both belonging and support. We&#39;re on a mission to change health care -- an experience made whole by our unique backgrounds and perspectives.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency:&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Final offer amounts, within the base pay set forth above, are determined by factors including your relevant skills, education, and experience. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Full-time employees are eligible for benefits including: medical, dental, and vision benefits, 11 paid holidays, paid sick time, paid parental leave, 401(k) plan participation, life and disability insurance, and paid wellness time and reimbursements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Artificial Intelligence (AI): &lt;/strong&gt;Our &lt;a href=&quot;https://oscarhealth.com/careers/ai-guidelines&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AI Guidelines&lt;/a&gt; outline the acceptable use of artificial intelligence for candidates and detail how we use AI to support our recruiting efforts.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasonable Accommodation: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Oscar applicants are considered solely based on their qualifications, without regard to applicant’s disability or need for accommodation. Any Oscar applicant who requires reasonable accommodations during the application process should contact the Oscar Benefits Team (accommodations@hioscar.com) to make the need for an accommodation known.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;California Residents:&lt;/strong&gt; For information about our collection, use, and disclosure of applicants’ personal information as well as applicants’ rights over their personal information, please see our &lt;a href=&quot;https://oscarhealth.com/privacy-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;From Fivetran’s founding until now, our mission has remained the same: to make access to data as simple and reliable as electricity. With Fivetran, customer data arrives in their warehouses, canonical and ready to query, with no engineering or maintenance required. We’re proud that more organizations continue to leverage our technology every day to become truly data-driven.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Customer Solutions Architect&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Customer Solutions Architect (Sr. CSA) owns the technical relationship for our most complex and strategic customers, helping them get the most value from the combined Fivetran and dbt platform. Working alongside Account Executives (AEs) and Solutions Engineers (SEs), the Sr. CSA makes sure these customers not only deploy successfully, but keep scaling and expanding their usage over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role operates as a technical account manager and strategic advisor to some of our largest customers. The Sr. CSA owns the technical narrative after go-live: leading architecture strategy, running executive-level technical conversations, uncovering new data challenges, and guiding customers through architecture evolution, adoption, and expansion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Sr. CSA is accountable for both retention and growth, and is measured on incremental ARR, Net Revenue Retention (NRR), and Gross Revenue Retention (GRR) across a book of larger, more strategic accounts. Beyond their own accounts, the Sr. CSA sets the standard for the CSA team by mentoring teammates, building repeatable playbooks, and shaping how the team works. This is a senior individual contributor role with no direct reports.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Austin, TX / Denver, CO / New York City, NY (hybrid). This is a full-time position, and candidates must be located in Austin, Denver or NYC and able to work in the office two days a week (Tuesday and Thursday).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Adoption and Value Realization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the post-sales technical relationship for a portfolio of our most complex, strategic Enterprise accounts, including multi-business-unit and multi-region customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the adoption strategy for each account, and drive optimization and sustained usage of the platform at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Introduce new products and features to customer leaders and architects, and shape how they fit into the customer&#39;s roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design enablement programs and workshops for large, distributed customer teams, and turn the best ones into reusable programs for the CSA team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate churn or contraction risks well before they surface, and lead recovery plans for at-risk strategic accounts, including implementation reviews and healthcheck sessions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expansion and Growth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-lead multi-quarter expansion strategy with the AE across business units, regions, and use cases, including opportunities to bring both Fivetran and dbt into an account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the account plan and own the technical side of the expansion pipeline, translating executive-level customer initiatives into scalable data workloads and solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical validation of the most complex new workloads, including workshops and, where necessary, proofs of concept (POCs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn successful use cases into repeatable expansion plays that other CSAs can run in their own accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on the customer lifecycle, renewals, and commercial structure of large accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Strategy and Architecture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the chief technical stakeholder for your accounts after go-live, and the escalation point for the hardest technical questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set architecture direction across your accounts, and design cross-product Fivetran and dbt reference architectures that other CSAs reuse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise customers&#39; senior architects and data leaders on pipelines, transformation, automation, governance, security, and platform adoption at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain technical artifacts such as architecture documentation, design patterns, and knowledge bases, and raise the quality bar for the team&#39;s shared assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Engagement and Account Planning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the company&#39;s technical voice with senior executives (VP and C-level), while building multi-threaded relationships across technical, operational, and executive stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run regular technical cadence calls, executive business reviews, and roadmap sessions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Mutual Success Plans and shape Mutual Account Plans with the AE, mapping whitespace across business units, subsidiaries, and use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align customer technical strategy with business objectives and commercial plans, and represent the technical view in account strategy discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internal and Partner Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the technical orchestrator across Sales, Professional Services, Product, and Engineering, resolving cross-team issues on strategic accounts with minimal direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for customer needs internally, and influence the product roadmap and priorities with well-supported customer evidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with technology partners and system integrators (e.g., Snowflake, Databricks, AWS, GCP) to drive joint value on strategic accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with CSA leadership to improve team processes, refine assets, and strengthen the knowledge-sharing loop&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Leadership Without Direct Reports&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and coach CSAs on technical depth, account strategy, and customer conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take on the most ambiguous and high-stakes customer situations, and bring structure that others can follow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a go-to expert and sounding board for complex accounts, architecture reviews, and executive-level presentations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help onboard new CSAs and contribute to hiring by interviewing candidates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and share playbooks, reference architectures, and demo assets that raise the performance of the whole team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Thought Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and deliver external-facing content through live events, speaking engagements, blog posts, recorded tutorials, or other educational resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the company as a technical speaker at customer, partner, and industry events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Regional and Product Marketing to support field and industry events, and align field and industry requirements with the product roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in a post-sales, customer-facing technical role, such as Solution Architect, Technical Account Manager, or Customer Success Engineer, with a track record on large Enterprise accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven record of owning customer outcomes after the sale, including adoption, renewal, and expansion, with results you can quantify (such as NRR, GRR, or incremental ARR)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep technical background, with experience designing scalable data architectures, a strong understanding of modern data warehousing and the analytics stack, and advanced SQL proficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate business objectives into technical solutions and measurable outcomes for complex, multi-team organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management skills across technical and non-technical audiences, and credibility presenting to senior executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring or coaching peers, and influencing teams and processes without formal authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, self-sufficient, and highly organized approach to managing multiple strategic accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating strategically while also engaging in deep technical discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate in an ambiguous, fast-paced environment, think on your feet in customer conversations, and bring structure to unclear situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A team-player mindset, both within the CSA team as we evolve our ways of working and in daily collaboration with AEs and SEs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Openness to travel: we value in-person relationship building, both internally and externally, and expect willingness to travel to customers and events as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Will Make You Stand Out&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with dbt, including large-scale project design; dbt certification is a bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python competency and advanced SQL knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud data platforms (Snowflake, Databricks, AWS, Azure, GCP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in data integration, ETL/ELT, or replication technologies, plus experience with ancillary tools, APIs, and managing data infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with workload-based or consumption-based sales models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with enterprise architecture frameworks and design patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with system integrators or technology partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience speaking at industry events or publishing technical content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technologies You’ll Use&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Databases: SAP HANA, Oracle, SQL Server, Postgres&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data platforms: Snowflake, Databricks, BigQuery, Redshift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Products: Fivetran, dbt platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Languages: SQL, Python, bash or PowerShell&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Networking: SSH tunneling, VPNs, PrivateLink&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modern data stack tools and ecosystem technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiring Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview with Talent Acquisition Partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview with Hiring Manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team Interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Final Interview: Mock Demo&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The compensation range displayed on this job posting reflects the minimum and maximum target for new hire compensation for the target position and level, and may include sales incentives or target bonuses depending on the role. For this role, on-target earnings (OTE) are split 80% base salary and 20% variable compensation. Our compensation ranges are determined by role, level, and location. Our job titles may span more than one career level. Within the range, individual compensation is determined by additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, relevant education or training, business need, market demands. The compensation range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. Your recruiter can share more about the specific compensation range for your location during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;OTE (On Target Earning)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$175,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$220,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot; style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Perks and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100% employer-paid medical insurance&lt;strong&gt;*&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Generous paid time away from work, including paid vacation or flexible/unlimited vacation depending on role and country, plus paid sick time, inclusive parental leave, paid holidays, including a year-end Global Week of Rest, and volunteer days off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RSU stock grants*&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional development and training opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company virtual happy hours, free food, and fun team-building activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly cell phone stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to an innovative mental health support platform that offers personalized care and resources in areas such as: therapy, coaching, and self-guided mindfulness exercises for all covered employees and their covered dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*&lt;/strong&gt;May vary by country and worker type - please reach out to your recruiter for more information&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1CdawUwjo1Q1B7ghZJ_owdmmHB8VtqhBu?usp=sharing&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about Fivetran&#39;s Benefits by Region.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;We’re honored to be &lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://fivetran.com/blog/hvr-acquisition-series-d&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://fivetran.com/blog/hvr-acquisition-series-d&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;valued at over $5.6 billion&lt;/a&gt;, but more importantly, we’re proud of our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://fivetran.com/culture&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://fivetran.com/culture&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;core values of Get Stuck In, Do the Right Thing, and One Team, One Dream&lt;/a&gt;. Read about us in&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://fivetran-com.s3.amazonaws.com/news/forbes-aug-sept-2022-digital-reprint-10-21-22.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://fivetran-com.s3.amazonaws.com/news/forbes-aug-sept-2022-digital-reprint-10-21-22.pdf&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Forbes&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;Fivetran brings together high-quality talent across the globe to make data access as easy and reliable as electricity for our customers. We value and recognize that our customers benefit from having innovative teams made of people from many backgrounds, experiences, and identities. Fivetran promotes diversity, equity, inclusion &amp;amp; belonging through attracting, recruiting, developing, and retaining a diverse workforce, not only because it is the right thing to do, but because it helps us build a world-class company to better serve our customers, our people and our communities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;To learn more about Fivetran’s culture and what it’s like to be part of the team, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xlhtp4dGh8o&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; and enjoy our video.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.3;&quot;&gt;To learn more about our candidate privacy policy, you can &lt;a href=&quot;https://fivetran.com/candidate-privacy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;read our statement here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
